# File Ingestion (`app/ingestor.py`)

Scans `SOURCE_PATH` and upserts questions + assets into the database based on filename patterns.

## Expected Folder Structure
```
SOURCE_PATH/
  <SUBJ>/
    PP/
      <SOURCE>/        # DSE, CE, AL
        <YEAR>/
          <PAPER>/     # P1, P2, etc.
            MATC_DSE_2024_P1_Q5_EN_QUE.png
    QB/
      <DETAIL>/        # e.g. MATHSMART2024
        MATC_QB_MATHSMART2024_Q1_EN_QUE.png
```

## Filename Patterns (Regex)
**Past Paper (PP):**
```
SUBJ_SOURCE_YEAR_PAPER_QNO_LANG_TYPE[_PART].EXT
MATC_DSE_2025_P2_Q5_EN_QUE.png
MATC_DSE_2025_P2_Q5_EN_QUE_2.png   ← part 2 of multi-image
```

**Question Bank (QB):**
```
SUBJ_QB_DETAIL_QNO_LANG_TYPE[_PART].EXT
MATC_QB_MATHSMART2024_Q1_EN_QUE.png
```

- `SUBJ`: subject ID (e.g. `MATC`, `MAT1`)
- `SOURCE`: `DSE`, `CE`, `AL`, `QB`
- `LANG`: `EN`, `CH`, `BI`
- `TYPE`: `QUE`, `ANS`, `SOL`
- `PART`: optional integer (default 1)
- `EXT`: `png`, `jpg`, `jpeg`, `gif`, `bmp` (→ IMG) or `doc`, `docx` (→ DOC)

## Auto Question Type Detection
Set at ingestion time based on subject + source + paper (only for MATC):
- `MATC DSE P1` → `CQ`
- `MATC DSE P2` → `MC`
- `MAT1/MAT2 DSE` → `CQ`
- All others → `NULL` (must be tagged manually)

## Key Functions
- `parse_filename(filename)` → dict or None
- `construct_qid(parsed)` → QID string
- `upsert_question(qid, parsed, folder_meta)` → Question object (create or fetch existing)
- `upsert_asset(question, parsed, file_path, source_path)` → insert or update asset
- `scan_directory(source_path)` → bulk ingest (CLI use)
- `scan_directory_stream(source_path, base_path)` → **generator** yielding progress dicts (UI/SSE use)
- `sync_database(source_path, dry_run)` → remove orphaned DB records
- `sync_database_stream(source_path, dry_run)` → **generator** yielding progress dicts (UI/SSE use)
- `find_untracked_files(source_path)` → files on disk with no DB record
- `get_database_stats(source_path)` → health statistics dict
- `preview_source_directory(source_path)` → folder tree summary

## Important: base_path vs source_path
When scanning a subject subfolder (e.g. `SOURCE_PATH/MATC`):
- Pass `source_path=SOURCE_PATH/MATC` (the dir to walk)
- Pass `base_path=SOURCE_PATH` (root for computing relative paths)

This ensures stored `file_path` values include the subject prefix: `MATC/PP/DSE/2024/P1/filename.png`

## Sync Grace Period
Questions created within the last **24 hours** are skipped during sync orphan checks. This prevents deleting questions that were just manually created but not yet had assets uploaded.

## File Path Convention
All `file_path` values stored in DB use **forward slashes** regardless of OS (normalised on ingest).
